  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (ja): オキナヨモギ",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%82%AA%E3%82%AD%E3%83%8A%E3%83%A8%E3%83%A2%E3%82%AE",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 109591405,
      "text": "オキナヨモギ は、キク科ヨモギ属に属する低木の一種である。オキナヨモギという和名は植物学者杉本順一が1965年に新たに与えたもので、別名にキダチヨモギがあり、また英名の1つの音写であるサザンウッドという呼び名も知られている。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (en): Artemisia abrotanum",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artemisia_abrotanum",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1368757332,
      "text": "Artemisia abrotanum, the southernwood, lad's love, or southern wormwood, is a species of flowering plant in the sunflower family. It is native to Eurasia and Africa but naturalized in scattered locations in North America. Other common names include: old man, boy's love, oldman wormwood, lover's plant, appleringie, garderobe, Our Lord's wood, maid's ruin, garden sagebrush, European sage, sitherwood and lemon plant."
    },
    "es": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (es): Artemisia abrotanum",
      "source_url": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artemisia_abrotanum",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 175080650,
      "text": "Artemisia abrotanum es una especie botánica perteneciente a la familia de las asteráceas. Es originaria de la región meridional de Europa, en especial de Italia y España."
    },
    "fr": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Artemisia abrotanum",
      "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artemisia_abrotanum",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 237971340,
      "text": "L’aurone ou citronnelle est une espèce de plantes herbacées vivaces de la famille des Astéracées, cultivée comme plante condimentaire et ornementale."
    },
    "pt": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (pt): Abrótano",
      "source_url": "https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abr%C3%B3tano",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 64323850,
      "text": "Abrótano (Artemisia abrotanum) é um nome comum de uma planta aromática da família Asteraceae encontrada na Europa, com propriedades medicinais. Também é conhecida por muitos nomes como \"aurónia\", \"losna\", \"abrótega\", \"abrótica\", \"abrótono\", \"alfacinha-do-rio\", \"artemísia\", \"erva-lombrigueira\"."
    },
    "id": {
      "source": "Wikipedia (id): Artemisia abrotanum",
      "source_url": "https://id.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artemisia_abrotanum",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 29410657,
      "text": "Artemisia abrotanum merupakan spesies tanaman berbunga dari famili Asteraceae yang berasal dari wilayah Eurasia dan Afrika, tetapi kini telah dinaturalisasi di berbagai lokasi di Amerika Utara. Tanaman ini dikenal memiliki aroma kuat menyerupai kapur barus dan secara tradisional dimanfaatkan sebagai pengharum ruangan alami maupun ramuan tabur. Bentuknya berupa semak kecil yang padat dan sering dibudidayakan karena nilai estetikanya di taman. Daunnya berwarna abu-abu kehijauan, berukuran kecil, sempit, serta ditutupi bulu halus, sementara bunganya berwarna kuning dan berukuran kecil. A. abrotanum dapat diperbanyak dengan mudah melalui stek batang atau pembelahan akar. Berkat keindahan dan kemudahan perawatannya, tanaman ini telah dianugerahi Award of Garden Merit oleh Royal Horticultural Society."
    }
  },
  "sections": {
    "cultivation": {
      "en": {
        "source": "Wikipedia (en): Artemisia abrotanum § Cultivation",
        "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artemisia_abrotanum#Cultivation",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
        "revision": 1368757332,
        "heading": "Cultivation",
        "text": "Artemisia abrotanum grows in acidic, well-drained soil and prefers loamy, sandy, clay soil to grow to full size. It needs full sun exposure in a sheltered location away from extreme winds. The plant is susceptible to root rot.",
        "truncated": false
      },
      "fr": {
        "source": "Wikipedia (fr): Artemisia abrotanum § Culture",
        "source_url": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artemisia_abrotanum#Culture",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
        "revision": 237971340,
        "heading": "Culture",
        "text": "Préfère un sol frais, bien drainé. Multiplication par division de touffes au printemps, ou éventuellement par bouturage.\nÀ chaque printemps, il convient de rabattre les touffes pour provoquer la repousse des feuilles.",
        "truncated": false
      }
    },
    "toxicity": {
      "en": {
        "source": "Wikipedia (en): Artemisia abrotanum § Toxicity",
        "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artemisia_abrotanum#Toxicity",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
        "revision": 1368757332,
        "heading": "Toxicity",
        "text": "In 2012, the European Food Safety Authority reported that all the aerial parts of Artemisia abrotanum contain substances that can be toxic to humans, due to the presence in the essential oil of bicyclic monoterpenes and phenylpropanoids. The severity of poison is low but if eaten in large quantities can be very toxic to humans. The parts of the plant that are poisonous are the bark, flowers, fruits, leaves, roots, seeds, and the stems.",
        "truncated": false
      }
    }
  },
